# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation

Successfully implemented Vercel Web Analytics for this React + Vite portfolio project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Installed @vercel/analytics package
- Added `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 as a dependency
- Package installed via npm, which is the project's package manager
- Updated package.json and package-lock.json accordingly

### 2. Integrated Analytics Component
Modified: `src/App.tsx`
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/react";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the main App component's JSX, just before the closing `</div>` tag
- Placement follows the official Vercel documentation for React/Vite applications

## Implementation Details

The integration follows the official Vercel Web Analytics quickstart guide for React/Vite projects:
- Used the React-specific package: `@vercel/analytics/react`
- Placed the Analytics component at the root level of the App component
- No additional configuration required - the component will automatically track page views and web vitals

## Verification Steps Completed

✅ Build completed successfully (npm run build)
✅ Linter passed with no errors (npm run lint)
✅ TypeScript compilation succeeded
✅ All dependencies installed correctly

## Next Steps for User

After deploying to Vercel:
1. Enable Web Analytics in your Vercel dashboard (Project Settings → Analytics → Enable)
2. Deploy the application to see analytics data
3. Analytics will start tracking page views and web vitals automatically
4. Verify tracking by checking browser Network tab for requests to `/_vercel/insights/*`

## Files Modified
- `portfo/package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `portfo/package-lock.json` - Updated lockfile with new dependency tree
- `portfo/src/App.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component
